.TH PI 1 "October 2026" "pi-coding-agent 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pi \- self-extensible AI coding agent for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pi
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ @files ...]
.RI [ messages ...]
.br
.B pi
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pi
is an interactive coding agent that runs in the terminal. It reads, edits,
and writes files, runs shell commands, and keeps persistent sessions, driving
a large language model through a tool-calling loop to carry out software
engineering tasks.
.PP
Run without arguments it starts an interactive session in the current
directory. Positional arguments are sent as the first message; arguments of
the form
.IB @ file
attach a file's contents to that message.
.PP
It talks to many providers through one unified API, including OpenAI,
Anthropic, Google, Mistral, Amazon Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, and GitHub Copilot,
and can be extended at runtime with custom tools, skills, prompt templates,
and themes.
.PP
Only the most common options are listed below; run
.B pi \-\-help
for the complete and authoritative list, which also includes flags
registered by loaded extensions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install \fIsource\fR
Install an extension source and add it to the settings.
.TP
.B remove \fIsource\fR
Remove an extension source from the settings
.RB ( uninstall
is an alias).
.TP
.B update \fR[\fIsource\fR|self|pi]
Update an extension, or pi itself. Note that when pi was installed from this
Debian package it should be updated through the system package manager rather
than with this command.
.TP
.B list
List the installed extensions.
.TP
.B config
Open the interactive UI to enable or disable package resources.
.TP
.B auth print-api-key\fR|\fBprint-bearer-token\fR|\fBcheck
Print a configured credential on stdout, or check provider readiness.
.B print-api-key
outputs the resolved API key;
.B print-bearer-token
outputs an OAuth bearer token (refreshing it if needed) with a default
30-minute minimum validity, adjustable with
.BR --min-expiry .
.B check
verifies that a provider is configured and refreshes expired OAuth
tokens; use
.B --no-refresh
to test without refreshing. All subcommands accept
.BI --provider " name"
and
.BI --model " pattern\&"
to select the credential source.
.TP
.B mcp add\fR|\fBremove\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBlogin\fR|\fBlogout
Manage MCP servers and their OAuth credentials. Configuration lives in
.I ~/.pi/agent/mcp.json
or a trusted project's
.IR .pi/mcp.json .
.B list
connects to enabled servers and reports their tools and connection errors.
Run
.B pi mcp --help
for command-specific options.
.SH OPTIONS
.BI \-\-provider " name"
Limit model selection to this provider. Requires
.BR --model .
.TP
.BI \-\-model " pattern"
Model pattern or ID; supports a
.RI \(dq provider / id \(dq
form and an optional
.RI \(dq : thinking \(dq
suffix.
.TP
.BI \-\-api\-key " key"
API key. Defaults to the provider's environment variable.
.TP
.BR \-\-print ", " \-p
Non-interactive mode: process the prompt, print the result, and exit.
A response truncated at the output token limit produces a warning and
non-zero exit status.
.TP
.BR \-\-continue ", " \-c
Continue the previous session.
.TP
.BR \-\-resume ", " \-r
Select a session to resume.
.TP
.BI \-\-session " path|id"
Use a specific session file or partial session UUID.
.TP
.BR \-\-thinking " " \fIlevel\fR
Set the reasoning effort: off, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, or max.
.TP
.BR \-\-tools ", " \-t " " \fItools\fR
Comma-separated allowlist of tool names or patterns (*) to enable.
Keeps MCP tools unless an entry starts with
.BR mcp__ .
A list containing only
.B +name
and
.B -name
entries adds to or removes from the default tools.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-tools ", " \-xt " " \fItools\fR
Comma-separated denylist of tool names or patterns (*) to disable,
including MCP tools.
.TP
.B \-\-no-mcp
Disable built-in MCP support: no servers connect and no MCP tools load.
.TP
.BR \-\-extension ", " \-e " " \fIpath\fR
Load an extension file or a built-in extension using
.BR builtin:name ;
may be given multiple times.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " file"
Export a session file to HTML and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Disable startup network operations (same as
.BR PI_OFFLINE=1 ).
.TP
.B \-\-
End option parsing; treat remaining arguments as messages or
.IB @ files\&,
allowing prompts that begin with a dash.
.TP
.BI \-\-tui-mode " mode"
TUI mode:
.BR fullscreen (default) or
.BR regular .
.TP
.BI \-\-use-theme " name"
Set the initial interactive theme for this run.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the full help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Show the version number and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PI_OFFLINE
When set to a non-empty value, disables startup network operations.
.TP
.B PI_CLIPBOARD_OSC52
Set to 1 to emit OSC 52 for text copies even if native clipboard commands succeed.
Useful when running remotely or inside a container; requires terminal support.
.PP
Provider credentials are read from their usual environment variables, for
example
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ,
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ,
or
.BR GEMINI_API_KEY .
See the provider documentation for the full list.
.SH CLIPBOARD
Clipboard text and image access on Linux use
.B wl-clipboard
on Wayland or
.B xclip
on X11. Install the matching optional package for desktop clipboard access.
Remote and headless text copy can use OSC 52 when supported by the terminal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pi/
Per-user configuration, settings, sessions, and discovered extensions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start an interactive session with an initial prompt:
.PP
.RS
.B pi \(dqList all .ts files in src/\(dq
.RE
.PP
Process a prompt non-interactively and exit:
.PP
.RS
.B pi \-p \(dqSummarize README.md\(dq
.RE
.PP
Use a specific provider and model:
.PP
.RS
.B pi \-\-model openai/gpt\-4o \(dqHelp me refactor this code\(dq
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Project website and documentation:
.UR https://pi.dev/
.UE .
.SH AUTHOR
Pi was written by Mario Zechner and contributors.
